# Was: BACKLOG #10 (the focused game's memory stays in sysmem), #9 (out and back in one step)
#
# CoD (pid 1684253) on monitor 1, Chrome/Claude/ghostty on monitor 2. At
# 11:50-11:57 the user works on monitor 2 and ~1 GB of CoD moves out; from
# 11:57:25 CoD is focused again but its memory comes back only at 12:05:22
# (recorded ram 989 MB the whole time; the simulator: 1002 MB), when the user
# lowered the settings. Not all of it can come back: CoD then wants ~10.3 GB
# and the rest of the desktop holds ~1.4 GB that cannot move, so ~900 MB of
# CoD has to be in sysmem either way (moved out, or new allocations turned
# away). Wanted: what fits comes back within seconds (the evicted part is the
# hot part: PCIe ran at 12-16 GB/s), no free memory left unused beyond the
# low mark while CoD has memory out, all of it back once there is room.
# ghostty and claude-desktop went out and back in the same step (11:57:40 in
